diff --git a/data/theme/luma-notifications/README.md b/data/theme/luma-notifications/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..af23565
--- /dev/null
+++ b/data/theme/luma-notifications/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+# Luma notification theme fragment
+
+These entry points compile only selectors owned by the Luma notification card,
+inline reply, and Shelf Beacon. They deliberately do not import the global
+GNOME Shell SCSS graph because the accepted checked-in Shell theme contains
+other independently accepted downstream surfaces that a full regeneration
+would overwrite.
+
+Compile each entry with `sassc -a INPUT OUTPUT`. Packaging compares the output
+against the matching notification-owned rules in `gnome-shell-dark.css`,
+`gnome-shell-light.css`, and `gnome-shell-high-contrast.css`; it must not replace
+the rest of those stylesheets with a full global SCSS regeneration.
+
+Run `verify-generated.sh` from this directory during packaging. It recompiles
+all three entries, byte-compares them with the checked-in fragments, and proves
+that each fragment is the literal suffix of the matching shipped stylesheet.
+
+`_material.scss` is the shared notification material ledger. Each entry changes
+only variant colors and accessibility overrides, while `_surface.scss` owns the
+complete selector set and geometry.
diff --git a/data/theme/luma-notifications/_material.scss b/data/theme/luma-notifications/_material.scss
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..fd65051
--- /dev/null
+++ b/data/theme/luma-notifications/_material.scss
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+// Standalone Luma notification material. These defaults are overridden only by
+// the three entry points in this directory; no GNOME-wide theme state is read.
+$note-ink: #e6eaec !default;
+$note-surface: rgba(38, 42, 48, .90) !default;
+$note-border: rgba(255, 255, 255, .085) !default;
+$note-summary-ink: #aeb5bb !default;
